        "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x-2y+4z=-3 \\\\ 2x+4y-8z=6 \\\\ -3x-6y+12z=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
        "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
