        "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-10y-5z=10 \\\\ -10x+100y+50z=-100 \\\\ -4x+40y+20z=-40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
        "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ -10 & 100 & 50 & -100 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ -10 & 100 & 50 & -100 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
